.page hello 1 greet Gensokyo from user space

# SYNOPSIS
*hello* [_ARGUMENT_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`hello` prints a greeting with its process id and user id, then lists its own arguments. It exists to check that a freshly built program can be loaded and run by the kernel, and that arguments reach it.

# EXAMPLES
    hello a "b c"

# SEE ALSO
utest(1), init(8)
